// BG-PRESERVE — server-side chat orchestration. Owned by the BG-PRESERVE patch (not
// upstream PocketRisu); registered from server.cjs via a single hooked line so an
// upstream update only needs `node bg-preserve-install.cjs apply` to re-register it.
//
// Purpose (§18.3/§18.6): run the entire sendChat pipeline (assembly → trigger/hypa →
// LLM → post) on the server as a fire-and-forget unit, so a backgrounded iOS tab can't
// suspend the ax→main handoff mid-flight.
//
// S1 (db input): handler reconstructs the server's view of the selected char/chat and
// compares against the client's unsaved currentChat. Verified.
//
// S2 (assembly): the server runs sendChat in PREVIEW mode (assembly only, returns right
// before the LLM call) using the bundled generation TS (bgOrchBundle.mjs, built from the
// live source by bgOrchBundle.build.cjs). This produces the server's `previewFormated` —
// the exact prompt array the client would send — so S2-C can byte-compare it against the
// client's. The bundle + node-only side packages (transformers tokenizer, wasmoon Lua) are
// loaded lazily on first use. Still no orchestration of a real generation, so the handler
