      // reply. The orchestrator does NOT depend on forageStorage for correctness — it builds the DB
      // from dbCache and returns results via the kv result channel — so present an EMPTY EPHEMERAL
      // store: auth passes, reads miss, writes are dropped. The in-memory hypaVectorCache still works
      // per-process, so embeddings are reused within a run and just recomputed across restarts.
      // Bonus: the no-op write also guards against the server pipeline accidentally clobbering the
      // real DB/storage files (results only flow back via kv → client merge → client save).
